#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:21
msgid "Intro to tilesets and tilemaps in Godot!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:22
msgid "LET'S GET STARTED!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:24
msgid "In this tour, you get an introduction to tilesets and tilemaps in Godot."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:28
msgid "You'll explore how [b]TileSet[/b] resources work like a painter's palette, and how [b]TileMapLayer[/b] nodes use that palette to paint levels."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:32
msgid "In the next tour, you'll start creating your own tileset from scratch."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:44
msgid "What are tilemaps?"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:47
msgid "Tilemaps are a widely used technique in 2D games to create levels and backgrounds."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:48
msgid "Instead of placing individual sprites, tilemaps let you paint your levels using collections of small images called [b]tiles[/b]."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:49
msgid "In this image, you can see tiles on the left and ivy painted on top of a platform using those tiles on the right:"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:56
msgid "Why use tilemaps?"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:59
msgid "There are several reasons to use tilemaps in your game:"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:61
msgid "You can paint your level structure intuitively"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:62
msgid "You need few art assets"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:63
msgid "Their performance is great"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:64
msgid "In Godot, tilemaps are feature-packed: collisions, AI pathfinding, and more are supported out of the box"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:70
msgid "Many games use tilemaps"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:73
msgid "Games that you know and love use tilemaps for their levels, including [b]Stardew Valley[/b], [b]Dead Cells[/b], or even [b]Hollow Knight[/b]!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:80
msgid "The environment in this screenshot from [b]Stardew Valley[/b] is made up of tiles: the dirt, fences, the grass are all tiles."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:86
msgid "This is a tilemap"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:93
msgid "This little game level I just opened is created entirely using Godot's tilemap system."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:94
msgid "Every platform, wall, and decoration you see in the environment is made up of tiles."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:95
msgid "Only the player character and the water plane use regular sprites."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:100
msgid "Run the scene"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:106
msgid "Run the scene to see the tilemap system in action!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:107
msgid "Click the [b]Run Current Scene[/b] button in the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:108
msgid "[b]Controls:[/b]"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:110
msgid "[b]Arrow keys[/b]: Move the character around"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:111
msgid "[b]C[/b]: Jump and double jump"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:113
msgid "Try jumping through the mushroom platforms! They are one-way platforms, so you can jump through them from below without falling through them from above."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:114
msgid "Close the game window when you're done exploring."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:120
msgid "Select the ground layer"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:126
msgid "Now that you've played the level, let's look at a [b]TileMapLayer[/b] node. This node is responsible for drawing tiles in the scene."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:127
msgid "Start by selecting the [b]TileMapLayer[/b] node named [b]Ground[/b] in the [b]Scene Dock[/b]."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:128
msgid "This node contains the main level structure: the floor and walls."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:134
msgid "The tilemap uses a grid"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:149
msgid "Great! Now let's look at the tilemap grid."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:150
msgid "The tilemap is organized into a grid where each square can hold exactly one tile. This ensures all tiles align perfectly."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:151
msgid "The grid also makes it easy to paint your level: you just click on a grid square to place a tile there."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:152
msgid "For this pixel art game, each grid square is 16x16 pixels to match the tile size."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:157
msgid "Multiple layers work together"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:163
msgid "Notice how this level uses multiple [b]TileMapLayer[/b] nodes. I selected two: [b]Ground[/b] and [b]Decorations[/b]."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:164
msgid "Each node represents one drawing layer and has a different purpose: the [b]Ground[/b] layer contains the main platforms and walls, while [b]Decorations[/b] adds little details like grass and mushrooms."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:165
msgid "You can use as many layers as you need to organize your level."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:170
msgid "The TileSet palette"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:175
msgid "But how does each [b]TileMapLayer[/b] know which tiles it can draw?"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:176
msgid "It uses a [b]TileSet[/b] resource. Think of it as a painter's palette containing all available tiles."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:177
msgid "Just like a painter chooses colors from their palette, the [b]TileMapLayer[/b] lets you pick tiles from its [b]TileSet[/b] to paint the level."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:178
msgid "Let's look at the [b]TileSet[/b] that contains all the mushroom world tiles."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:183
msgid "TileMapLayer nodes use the Tileset resource"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:188
msgid "Here's how the tilemap system works. You:"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:189
msgid "1. Create a [b]TileSet[/b] resource (your palette of tiles)"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:190
msgid "2. Assign the [b]TileSet[/b] to a [b]TileMapLayer[/b] node in the [b]Inspector[/b]"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:191
msgid "3. Use the [b]TileMapLayer[/b] to paint your level with tiles from the [b]TileSet[/b]"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:192
msgid "You can see the [b]TileSet[/b] assigned to the [b]Ground[/b] layer in the [b]Inspector[/b]."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:197
msgid "Open the TileSet editor"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:203
msgid "The [b]TileSet[/b] editor is where you create and configure your palette of tiles."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:204
msgid "Click the [b]TileSet button[/b] at the bottom to switch from the [b]TileMap editor[/b] to the [b]TileSet editor[/b]."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:205
msgid "You'll see the actual tiles that make up this mushroom world."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:209
msgid "Open the TileSet editor."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:216
msgid "What's in a TileSet?"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:220
msgid "A [b]TileSet[/b] resource contains all the data needed to draw tiles:"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:222
msgid "Tile textures (the actual images)"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:223
msgid "Collision shapes for physics"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:224
msgid "Terrain rules for auto-connecting tiles"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:225
msgid "Custom properties for each tile"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:227
msgid "The [b]TileSet[/b] editor exposes all of that."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:232
msgid "Your tile palette"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:236
msgid "Here's the [b]TileSet[/b] palette used to create the level you just played!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:237
msgid "The interface is busy but you can see individual tiles for the ground on the right side."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:238
msgid "Each tile here can be painted onto a [b]TileMapLayer[/b] to build your level."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:239
msgid "In the next tours, you'll learn how to create your own [b]TileSet[/b] like this one."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:246
msgid "Excellent!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:247
msgid "CONTINUE"
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:249
msgid "Great work! You now understand how [b]TileSets[/b] and [b]TileMapLayers[/b] work together."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:252
msgid "Remember: the [b]TileSet[/b] is your palette of tiles and the [b]TileMapLayer[/b] where you paint with those tiles."
msgstr ""

#: tours/101_overview/101_overview.gd:255
msgid "In the next tour, you'll create your first [b]TileSet[/b] from scratch and start building your own levels!"
msgstr ""
